COMMAND "Add a JS SDK Client Method" DESCRIPTION "Land a new @barkpark/core client method end-to-end — the six-file layer-parity chore the SDK repeats ~3x/month (34 commits in 12 months touch types.ts + client.ts + index.ts together): a starter module wrapping a dataset-scoped GET in the house transport pattern, Result/Options types plus the BarkparkClient interface signature, the createClient wiring entry, both index.ts barrel exports, an msw test pair, and the changesets entry the js/ CI gate requires — the corpus's first changeset-creating command. Idempotent behind six per-method marks; every anchor is a never-consumed fixed line, so no REANCHOR families are needed." LAST_UPDATED "17-07-2026-14-00-00" DOMAIN "barkpark" TAGS "sdk", "scaffold", "testing" CONCEPT "sdk-method" VARIANT "ts-read" DIRECTION "add" VARIABLES
  VARIABLE 1 "MethodName" TITLE "Name the client method" DESCRIPTION "The method's name, declared PascalCase and rendered per position (A1): {{.methodName}} (camel) is the client method AND the module's exported function — the house wiring shadow, client.ts's `getBacklinks(id, opts) { return getBacklinks(frozen, id, opts) }` idiom; {{.method-name}} (kebab) is the module filename (image-url.ts precedent), the test filename, the changeset slug and every mark suffix. Pick a verb-first name like the 30+ live methods (get*/list*/search*/export*)." EXAMPLES "GetUsageReport", "ListLocales", "GetDatasetHealth"
  VARIABLE 2 "TypeBase" TITLE "Base name for the public types" DESCRIPTION "PascalCase noun stem for the two new public types, {{.TypeBase}}Result and {{.TypeBase}}Options — the BacklinksResult/BacklinksOptions convention. Deliberately a SEPARATE variable from MethodName: the live corpus derives type names from the noun, not the verb (getAnalytics returns DatasetAnalytics, getBacklinks returns BacklinksResult), and that judgment cannot be a casing transform." EXAMPLES "UsageReport", "Locales", "DatasetHealth"
  VARIABLE 3 "HttpPath" OPAQUE TITLE "The dataset-scoped API path prefix" DESCRIPTION "The v1 route WITHOUT the trailing dataset segment — the method appends /:dataset itself, exactly like analytics.ts:21 builds `${scopePrefix(config)}/v1/data/analytics/${encodeURIComponent(config.dataset)}`. Leading slash, no trailing slash. OPAQUE: verbatim, never re-cased, one token spelling ({{.HttpPath}}) throughout." EXAMPLES "/v1/data/usage", "/v1/data/locales", "/v1/data/health"
  VARIABLE 4 "Summary" OPAQUE TITLE "One-line method summary" DESCRIPTION "What the method fetches, one clause, lowercase start, no trailing period — it is spliced mid-sentence into the JSDoc on the module function, the types, the interface signature, and the changeset body. OPAQUE: verbatim prose, ASCII, no braces or backticks." EXAMPLES "the dataset's usage report", "the locales configured for the dataset"

# ===========================================================================
# add-sdk-method — the SDK layer-parity chore, mechanized.
#
# PRIOR ART & EVIDENCE (the 2026-07-17 anchor survey). Every new capability
# grows the same six-file cluster, measured at 34 commits in 12 months
# (~3/month) touching js/packages/core/src/{types,client,index}.ts together —
# getSearchSuggestions (#873), listDatasets (#732), getAnalytics (#706),
# exportDataset (#696), webhook mgmt (#604), searchAssets (#585)… Each commit
# lands: a per-concern module under src/ (analytics.ts, export.ts), the
# Result/Options types + a BarkparkClient signature in types.ts, an import +
# wiring entry in client.ts, a value export + type re-export in index.ts, an
# msw test under tests/, and a js/.changeset/ entry (the changesets CI job
# blocks packages/** PRs without one — js/CLAUDE.md hard rule). README is NOT
# part of the shape: all five exemplar commits touch zero READMEs.
#
# WHY NO REANCHOR FAMILIES (the survey's key structural finding). Unlike the
# oban crontab and the @hints map — whose last elements carry no trailing
# separator, forcing the A3 self-consuming REPLACE + REANCHOR — every accretion
# site here is either newline-separated (import lines, export lines, interface
# members) or a collection whose EVERY entry carries a trailing comma (the
# createClient object literal, index.ts's export-type block: house prettier
# style). So all six injections are bare INSERT AFTER FIRST against a FIXED
# anchor line that is never consumed, each payload plants its own per-method
# mark, and idempotency is the engine's implicit planted-MARK guard — a re-run
# with the same MethodName sees MARK:sdk-…-<method-name> and skips. Sibling
# accretion is LIFO after the same anchors (the add-error-shape Op B/C idiom),
# which is safe because ordering is neutral at every site: object property
# order, interface member order, export order and import order are all
# semantically irrelevant in TS.
#
# THE SIX ANCHORS, grep-proven unique (2026-07-17):
#   client.ts:22    import { getBacklinks } from './backlinks'
#   client.ts:280   const client: BarkparkClientWithHandshake = {
#   types.ts:16     export type Perspective = 'published' | 'drafts' | 'raw'
#   types.ts:1044   export interface BarkparkClient {
#   index.ts:16     export { createClient } from './client'
#   index.ts:187      ApiVersion,   (the './types' block's first member)
#
# WHY NO Verb ONEOF (ruled out, with evidence). 27 of the 34 surveyed commits
# are GET reads; the write-shaped minority (upsertSchema PUT, createWorkspace
# POST, webhook CRUD) diverges STRUCTURALLY, not lexically — `kind: 'write'`,
# a body, a MutateEnvelope unwrap, different test fixtures. Scaffy payloads
# are conditional-free text, so a Verb enum would demand per-verb payload
# bodies the grammar cannot express. The starter therefore scaffolds the
# dominant shape — a token-scoped dataset GET in the analytics/backlinks
# transport idiom — and the module body carries a fenced TODO explaining the
# write flip (kind, method, body) for the author to make by hand.
#
# ORDER DEPENDENCY, DELIBERATE. tsc's excess-property check means the
# createClient object literal may only carry the method once BarkparkClient
# declares it — so the types.ts signature op precedes the client.ts wiring op,
# and the tsc gate at the bottom is what catches any drift between them.
# ===========================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OP 1 — the starter module. Compiles and RUNS as-is: dataset-scoped GET via
# the house transport (scopePrefix + request + tolerant `result ?? data`
# unwrap — the getSearchSuggestions/getBacklinks idiom), AbortSignal plumbed.
# The permissive Result starter and the write-flip note are fenced TODOs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CREATE FILE IF ABSENT "js/packages/core/src/{{.method-name}}.ts"
WITH
::: {{.method-name}} module :::
// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// Copyright 2026 Barkpark contributors

// {{.TypeBase}} — fetches {{.Summary}} (`GET {{.HttpPath}}/:dataset`).
// A token-scoped dataset read in the house transport idiom (analytics.ts,
// backlinks.ts). scaffy:add-sdk-method starter — refine the response typing in
// types.ts ({{.TypeBase}}Result), then delete this pointer comment.
//
// TODO(scaffy:add-sdk-method) if this method should WRITE instead of read:
// switch reqOpts to `{ kind: 'write', method: 'POST', body: … }`, return the
// MutateEnvelope shapes, and mirror a write exemplar (schemas.ts upsertSchema)
// rather than this read skeleton.

import { scopePrefix } from './scope'
import { request } from './transport'
import type { BarkparkClientConfig, {{.TypeBase}}Result, {{.TypeBase}}Options } from './types'

/**
 * Fetch {{.Summary}} (`GET {{.HttpPath}}/:dataset`).
 * Prefer `client.{{.methodName}}()`.
 */
export async function {{.methodName}}(
  config: BarkparkClientConfig,
  opts?: {{.TypeBase}}Options,
): Promise<{{.TypeBase}}Result> {
  const path = `${scopePrefix(config)}{{.HttpPath}}/${encodeURIComponent(config.dataset)}`
  const reqOpts: { kind: 'read'; signal?: AbortSignal } = { kind: 'read' }
  if (opts?.signal !== undefined) reqOpts.signal = opts.signal
  const { data } = await request<{{.TypeBase}}Result & { result?: {{.TypeBase}}Result }>(
    config,
    path,
    reqOpts,
  )
  return (data.result ?? data) as {{.TypeBase}}Result
}
::: {{.method-name}} module :::

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OP 2 — the msw test pair, byte-shaped on analytics.test.ts: one happy-path
# (route hit + unwrap) and one error-propagation case, against the shared
# fixtures server. Self-contained — the fixture imports carry all setup.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CREATE FILE IF ABSENT "js/packages/core/tests/{{.method-name}}.test.ts"
WITH
::: {{.method-name}} test :::
import { afterAll, afterEach, beforeAll, describe, expect, it } from 'vitest'
import { http, HttpResponse } from 'msw'
import { server } from './fixtures/server'
import { TEST_BASE_URL, TEST_DATASET, resetFixtures } from './fixtures/handlers'
import { createClient } from '../src/client'
import type { BarkparkClientConfig } from '../src/types'

const baseConfig: BarkparkClientConfig = {
  projectUrl: TEST_BASE_URL,
  dataset: TEST_DATASET,
  apiVersion: '2026-04-17',
  token: 't',
}

beforeAll(() => server.listen({ onUnhandledRequest: 'error' }))
afterEach(() => {
  server.resetHandlers()
  resetFixtures()
})
afterAll(() => server.close())

describe('{{.methodName}}', () => {
  it('GETs {{.HttpPath}}/:dataset and unwraps the payload', async () => {
    let seenPath = ''
    server.use(
      http.get(`${TEST_BASE_URL}{{.HttpPath}}/:ds`, ({ request }) => {
        seenPath = new URL(request.url).pathname
        return HttpResponse.json({ ok: true })
      }),
    )
    const bp = createClient(baseConfig)
    const res = await bp.{{.methodName}}()
    expect(res.ok).toBe(true)
    expect(seenPath).toContain(`{{.HttpPath}}/${TEST_DATASET}`)
  })

  it('propagates a server error', async () => {
    server.use(
      http.get(`${TEST_BASE_URL}{{.HttpPath}}/:ds`, () =>
        HttpResponse.json({ error: { code: 'unauthorized' } }, { status: 401 }),
      ),
    )
    const bp = createClient(baseConfig)
    await expect(bp.{{.methodName}}()).rejects.toThrow()
  })
})
::: {{.method-name}} test :::

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OP 3 — the public types. Anchored right after the Perspective alias
# (types.ts:16, unique, never consumed) — exactly where ExportOptions landed
# in the exportDataset exemplar. The Result starter is deliberately
# permissive ([key: string]: unknown) so the slice compiles before the author
# types the real fields; the TODO says so out loud.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
IN "js/packages/core/src/types.ts"
### Declare {{.TypeBase}}Result + {{.TypeBase}}Options after the Perspective alias
INSERT AFTER FIRST
::: perspective alias :::
export type Perspective = 'published' | 'drafts' | 'raw'
::: perspective alias :::
WITH
::: {{.TypeBase}} types :::

// scaffy:add-sdk-method {{.method-name}} MARK:sdk-types-{{.method-name}}
/** Result of `client.{{.methodName}}()` — {{.Summary}} (`GET {{.HttpPath}}/:dataset`). */
export interface {{.TypeBase}}Result {
  // TODO(scaffy:add-sdk-method): replace this permissive starter with the
  // endpoint's real response fields (see DatasetAnalytics / BacklinksResult).
  [key: string]: unknown
}

/** Options for `client.{{.methodName}}()`. */
export interface {{.TypeBase}}Options {
  /** AbortSignal to cancel the request. */
  signal?: AbortSignal
}
::: {{.TypeBase}} types :::
MARK "sdk-types-{{.method-name}}"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OP 4 — the BarkparkClient signature, inserted right after the interface
# opening (types.ts:1044, unique). Interface member order is semantically
# neutral; landing at the head keeps the anchor never-consumed. Must precede
# Op 6 (see ORDER DEPENDENCY above).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
IN "js/packages/core/src/types.ts"
### Declare client.{{.methodName}}() on the BarkparkClient interface
INSERT AFTER FIRST
::: BarkparkClient opening :::
export interface BarkparkClient {
::: BarkparkClient opening :::
WITH
::: {{.methodName}} signature :::
  // scaffy:add-sdk-method {{.method-name}} MARK:sdk-signature-{{.method-name}}
  /** Fetch {{.Summary}} (`GET {{.HttpPath}}/:dataset`). */
  {{.methodName}}(opts?: {{.TypeBase}}Options): Promise<{{.TypeBase}}Result>
::: {{.methodName}} signature :::
MARK "sdk-signature-{{.method-name}}"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OP 5 — the client.ts import. Import lines are newline-separated, so a bare
# INSERT after the (unique, stable) backlinks import is separator-safe.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
IN "js/packages/core/src/client.ts"
### Import {{.methodName}} from its module
INSERT AFTER FIRST
::: backlinks import :::
import { getBacklinks } from './backlinks'
::: backlinks import :::
WITH
::: {{.methodName}} import :::
// scaffy:add-sdk-method {{.method-name}} MARK:sdk-import-{{.method-name}}
import { {{.methodName}} } from './{{.method-name}}'
::: {{.methodName}} import :::
MARK "sdk-import-{{.method-name}}"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OP 6 — the createClient wiring, inserted right after the object-literal
# opening (client.ts:280, unique). Every entry in the literal carries a
# trailing comma, and property order is neutral, so the head slot is as valid
# as the tail. The method-shorthand body calls the IMPORTED {{.methodName}}
# (shorthand creates no shadowing binding — the live getBacklinks idiom).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
IN "js/packages/core/src/client.ts"
### Wire client.{{.methodName}}() in createClient
INSERT AFTER FIRST
::: client literal opening :::
  const client: BarkparkClientWithHandshake = {
::: client literal opening :::
WITH
::: {{.methodName}} wiring :::
    // scaffy:add-sdk-method {{.method-name}} MARK:sdk-wire-{{.method-name}}
    {{.methodName}}(opts) {
      return {{.methodName}}(frozen, opts)
    },
::: {{.methodName}} wiring :::
MARK "sdk-wire-{{.method-name}}"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OP 7 — the index.ts value export (the composable-without-createClient
# surface every module also ships). Newline-separated export lines; the
# createClient export (index.ts:16) is the file's head anchor.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
IN "js/packages/core/src/index.ts"
### Barrel-export {{.methodName}} from the package root
INSERT AFTER FIRST
::: createClient export :::
export { createClient } from './client'
::: createClient export :::
WITH
::: {{.methodName}} export :::
// scaffy:add-sdk-method {{.method-name}} MARK:sdk-export-{{.method-name}}
export { {{.methodName}} } from './{{.method-name}}'
::: {{.methodName}} export :::
MARK "sdk-export-{{.method-name}}"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OP 8 — the index.ts type re-export, inserted after the './types' block's
# first member (`  ApiVersion,` — unique in the file). Every member of the
# block carries a trailing comma and the list is order-neutral, so a bare
# INSERT is separator-safe; a `//` comment line is legal inside an
# `export type { … }` block.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
IN "js/packages/core/src/index.ts"
### Re-export the {{.TypeBase}} types from the package root
INSERT AFTER FIRST
::: ApiVersion member :::
  ApiVersion,
::: ApiVersion member :::
WITH
::: {{.TypeBase}} type re-export :::
  // scaffy:add-sdk-method {{.method-name}} MARK:sdk-type-export-{{.method-name}}
  {{.TypeBase}}Result,
  {{.TypeBase}}Options,
::: {{.TypeBase}} type re-export :::
MARK "sdk-type-export-{{.method-name}}"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OP 9 — the changeset, a corpus first. The js/ CI `changesets` job BLOCKS any
# packages/** PR without one (js/CLAUDE.md hard rule), and every exemplar
# commit ships exactly this shape (sdk-export-dataset.md, sdk-get-analytics.md
# …): front-matter bumping @barkpark/core minor + one **Added:** line. A new
# public method is semver-minor by definition, so the bump is mechanical — no
# judgment left for a manual step.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CREATE FILE IF ABSENT "js/.changeset/sdk-{{.method-name}}.md"
WITH
::: {{.method-name}} changeset :::
---
'@barkpark/core': minor
---

**Added:** `client.{{.methodName}}(opts?)` — fetches {{.Summary}} (`GET {{.HttpPath}}/:dataset`). New `{{.TypeBase}}Result` / `{{.TypeBase}}Options` public types.
::: {{.method-name}} changeset :::

# ===========================================================================
# POSTCONDITIONS. ASSERT FILE: every planted mark plus the load-bearing lines
# of the created files (payload-derived, ASCII, brace-safe — each `}}` is a
# token closing followed by `R`, `O`, `(`, `.` or a quote, never `}`).
# ===========================================================================
ASSERT FILE "js/packages/core/src/{{.method-name}}.ts" CONTAINS "export async function {{.methodName}}("
ASSERT FILE "js/packages/core/tests/{{.method-name}}.test.ts" CONTAINS "describe('{{.methodName}}'"
ASSERT FILE "js/packages/core/src/types.ts" CONTAINS "MARK:sdk-types-{{.method-name}}"
ASSERT FILE "js/packages/core/src/types.ts" CONTAINS "MARK:sdk-signature-{{.method-name}}"
ASSERT FILE "js/packages/core/src/client.ts" CONTAINS "MARK:sdk-import-{{.method-name}}"
ASSERT FILE "js/packages/core/src/client.ts" CONTAINS "MARK:sdk-wire-{{.method-name}}"
ASSERT FILE "js/packages/core/src/index.ts" CONTAINS "MARK:sdk-export-{{.method-name}}"
ASSERT FILE "js/packages/core/src/index.ts" CONTAINS "MARK:sdk-type-export-{{.method-name}}"
ASSERT FILE "js/.changeset/sdk-{{.method-name}}.md" CONTAINS "'@barkpark/core': minor"

# Run gates — all LOCAL per the proven tier table: the pnpm bootstrap is THE
# precondition for the tsc + vitest gates in a fresh worktree (103 phantom
# errors -> 0), the scoped vitest run exercises exactly the created test pair,
# and tsc --noEmit is what catches signature/wiring drift (the ORDER
# DEPENDENCY tripwire). The full cross-package suite, lint sweep and size
# budget stay on the js-tests.yml CI gate.
ASSERT CMD "cd js && pnpm install && pnpm --filter @barkpark/core build"
ASSERT CMD "cd js/packages/core && npx vitest run tests/{{.method-name}}.test.ts"
ASSERT CMD "cd js/packages/core && npx tsc --noEmit"
